    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="0c57d9fc-ebcc-58f7-981d-8e47a8cfa373" activityNameId="c8bfda95-9eea-5629-8c40-749d8550b29a" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Transoceanic freight ship</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Transoceanic freight ship
The exchanges of the ship manufacturing are derived from an assessment of a spip, with a load capacity of 51'500t. Energy consumption in manufacturing was estimated as 50% of the cumulative energy of the used materials. The split of energies is 10% electricity and 90% heavy fuel oil.;
UUID: 05074e10-3d3d-30e2-86f9-938244496b81
This inventory calls processes of material production, representing the material composition of an average water vehicle used for solid goods transportation. For manufacturing, electricity and heavy oil burned in industrial furnace are included. For the transportation of materials standandard distance are applied. Also, waste treatment processes for non metal components of a water vehicle are accounted for.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: container ship
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: literature studies and own calculations. 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_05074e10-3d3d-30e2-86f9-938244496b81.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
